WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.380
- Last year it was the 25th
anniversary of "Clueless".

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.850
I know that you have had
to talk to about this film,

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:05.680
like I talk about "Since
You've Been Gone" in my career,

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.130
so I get that you're probably over it,

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:10.370
but I will say the very first
car I ever bought myself

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:11.371
was because of you.

00:00:11.371 --> 00:00:12.510
- Did you get the white Jeep?
- And it was the white Jeep.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:13.650
Yep, like everyone else.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:14.872
I was not, I was a basic bitch.

00:00:14.872 --> 00:00:15.800
(laughing)

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:19.341
But I was like I want that Jeep so badly.

00:00:19.341 --> 00:00:20.910
But do you still keep up?

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.810
It was such a great
cast and a lot of y'all

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:24.430
gone to do so many amazing things.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.030
So like, do you still keep
up with the castmates or no?

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.240
- We hadn't seen each other
in a really long time.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.830
And then Donald Faison and Breckin Meyer

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:34.770
and Paul Rudd and I all went to Chicago

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.420
about a year ago or something.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.570
And being, I was so lucky
to be with those three.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.220
There they are, the Goofies.
- [Kelly] That's so awesome.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.770
- They are so funny.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.032
And they made fun of me a lot

00:00:44.032 --> 00:00:46.840
because we all had to go on
stage to talk about the film

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.410
and Breckin and Donald were talking,

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.390
well, Donald was talking
about this birthday party

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:54.780
that he had and saying that I was there

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.310
and remember this and remember that.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:57.850
And I didn't remember any of it.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.410
And Paul Rudd at one point turned to me

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:00.860
'cause then he was
talking about another part

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.150
of the movie and he said,
were you even there?

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:04.943
Like, do you remember the movie?

00:01:04.943 --> 00:01:06.411
- I said, I do, I do.

00:01:06.411 --> 00:01:08.910
But I had the best time with those guys.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:10.920
They're so funny and so sweet.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.260
- But it's interesting that you say that

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.570
because I don't remember
everything either,

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.550
but it's, and you don't
know that you're gonna be

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:18.820
a part of one of the biggest
movies in pop culture.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.990
You know, you don't know
that when you're shooting it.

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:22.197
You're not like, "I must hold onto this

00:01:22.197 --> 00:01:23.337
"'cause this will, I will be talking

00:01:23.337 --> 00:01:24.380
"about this in 30 years."

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:25.240
Like, you know what I'm saying?

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:26.490
You don't, you don't think like that

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.191
but it's such an unforgettable,
such a great movie.

00:01:29.191 --> 00:01:30.730
- Thank you.
- So you have two movies,

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:32.960
two new movies coming out, so you're busy.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.500
And can you tell us about them?

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.750
- Yeah, so one of them
is "(beep) Hits the Fan"

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.409
and another--
- Which is a great title.

00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:41.230
- Yeah, I mean, it's really,

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:44.660
that's an interesting sort
of thriller film, sexy.

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:46.780
I can't wait to see that come together.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:49.700
And then "The Requin"
which is an adventure

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:54.700
or more a survival kind of, with a shark.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:56.461
- I am in.
- The requiem shark.

00:01:56.461 --> 00:01:59.340
And I got so hurt making this movie

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.560
and it was so freezing cold
and it was so exciting.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:02.620
It was the time of my life.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.160
'Cause this director is incredible.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:05.230
- Why did you get so hurt?

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:07.860
- Oh, 'cause I'm not in shape and--

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:10.312
- Oh, I am.
(laughing)

00:02:10.312 --> 00:02:11.930
I'm so pristine.
- I'm not quite in shape.

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:13.910
I'm not an, it wasn't
like an, I didn't realize

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.640
that it was an action film
until I was doing it, you know?

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:19.930
And anyway, so that one is, I can't wait.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.860
And then "Baby-Sitter's Club 2".

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:23.720
So I just finished shooting that, yeah.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:24.630
- That's so cool.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.137
So many cool nostalgic things.

